			"Message": "style(Mountain): Strip AI-internal annotations and reorganize Cargo features\n\nRemove emoji markers (🟠🔵) and the .hermes/microsoft/ doc reference path\nfrom the Shim module comment, keeping only the functional description of the\ngated interception layer. Relocate inline Shim tier explanatory comments from\nthe default features list in Cargo.toml.\n\nReorganize feature flags into logical groups — tier flags, subsystem\nfeatures, and the Shim gate — for better maintainability alongside the\nexisting declarations per project policy on source cleanliness.",
			"SHA": "0b9e8f0ca5e36019d5a812f965861eb01b7d668e"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T22:20:44Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1865,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add Shim module with Gate and SwallowMap for IPC interception\n\nEstablish the Rust-level foundation for the deep-shim interception layer introduced by the TierShim env-var in the prior commit. Two new modules live behind the `pub mod Shim` declaration in Library.rs:\n\n- **Gate** — Compile-time tier gate reading `env!(\"TierShim\")` (baked by build.rs via EmitTierDefaults), exporting boolean guards (`is_enabled`, `is_proxy`, `is_replace_or_deeper`, `is_own_or_preempt`, `is_preempt`) that drive `#[cfg]` gating throughout Mountain. Zero overhead at default `None` tier via dead-code elimination.\n\n- **SwallowMap** — Pattern-matching decision engine that maps IPC method names (e.g. `statusbar:`, `telemetry:`) to a `SwallowAction`/`RedirectTarget` pair, determining whether Mountain handles the call locally, forwards it to Wind/Cocoon/Output/Sky, or discards it entirely (telemetry). Rules are checked in insertion order; first match wins with a default `Passthrough → None` fallback.\n\nCargo.toml gains inline comments documenting the four active shim tiers and their corresponding Rust features. This completes the Rust-side routing infrastructure for the Land Shim plan.\n\nSee: `.hermes/microsoft/05-Mountain-Rust-Intercept.md`",
			"SHA": "d22f305e382b83b58e9a6ac5f32ce87c7369afc3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:54:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add TierShim env-var for deep-hook intercept layer\n\nIntroduce a new `TierShim` compile-time environment variable to build.rs that enables an experimental deep-hook intercept layer for VS Code service instantiation. The tier defines five progressive levels compiled out via `#[cfg]` gates:\n\n- `None` — zero overhead, all shim code omitted (default)\n- `Proxy` — audit-only observation of existing paths\n- `Replace` — individual service shim replacement\n- `Own` — Land owns the InstantiationService container\n- `Preempt` — Land controls BrowserMain.open()\n\nAdd the default emission in EmitTierDefaults and wire validation into IsDefaultTierValue. No behavioral change at default `None`.",
			"SHA": "885383348767e1ef23c19da1124877eadf237a49"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:41:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Fire onFileSystem activation on register_file_system_provider\n\nExtract `register_file_system_provider` from the catch-all handler group and give it a dedicated match arm that fires `$activateByEvent(\"onFileSystem:{scheme}\")` when an extension registers a virtual file-system provider. The scheme is read from the `scheme` key in the parameters object.\n\nThis ensures extensions declaring `\"activationEvents\": [\"onFileSystem:xyz\"]` in their manifest are activated on registration, matching VS Code's behaviour. The provider is still forwarded through `RegisterLanguageProvider` for handle tracking, and a warning is logged when the provider falls outside the known language-feature map.",
			"SHA": "9f2f1783e8d68a4825ed628969e4297d12606d05"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T21:23:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1861,
				1
			],
			"Message": "style(Mountain): Fix indentation of diagnostic:getBootMarks match arm in DispatchMatch\n\nThe `diagnostic:getBootMarks` handler and its preceding doc comment were indented one tab level deeper than the surrounding match arms in `mountain_ipc_invoke`, creating an inconsistent brace depth relative to the other cases.\n\nDedent the arm and comment block by one level to align with the enclosing match statement's formatting. No behavioral change.",
			"SHA": "9262422ce1ef71be84be4d5edeafe56025bdba8e"
		}
